            }
          },
          "description": "EXACT spherical cell-area weight over the lat (cell) axis: latcell_area[gja] = sin(pi/180 * phie[gja+1]) - sin(pi/180 * phie[gja]), gathering the consumer's NLAT+1-node degree-valued edge array phie. This is the exact integral of cos(phi) dphi across the cell, not a midpoint approximation, so the flux-form meridional divergence (F[j+1] coslat_edge[j+1] - F[j] coslat_edge[j]) / latcell_area[j] telescopes to an exact global mass budget. Positive when dlat_deg > 0. The physical cell area on a sphere of radius R is R^2 dlon_rad latcell_area[gja]. At the two half-polar caps latcell_area ~ dphi^2/8 — SECOND order small in the grid spacing while the adjacent face is only FIRST order small (coslat_edge ~ dphi/2); that O(1/dphi) amplification is why near-pole convergence requires the product V dq/dphi to vanish like cos(phi) at the pole (see grids/latlon3d/rules/upwind1_flux_D_lat_polar). Aggregate index `gja`, distinct from the producer's `gje` — with a shared name the offset gather phie[gja+1] is captured and silently degenerates to phie[gja], returning EXACT ZEROS (see the AGGREGATE-INDEX HYGIENE paragraph in metadata.description).",
          "params": [
            "phie"
          ]
        },
